fix(memory): auto-capture ran on Anthropic path only + swallowed errors silently

Mason: clean answer, no tool spam (prompt fix held), but NO "remembered"
note. Root cause: the auto-capture hook was inline on the Anthropic path's
fall-through return ONLY. The local-model path and OpenAI path have their own
early `return Ok(messages)` that never reached it. And every branch swallowed
errors, so a silent no-op gave zero diagnosis.

- Extract run_auto_capture() shared helper; call it from ALL three provider
  return paths (local, OpenAI, Anthropic).
- It now LOGS every branch to the terminal: OFF / no-vault-scope / no-Memory-
  dir / embedder-unavailable / "N candidates -> C created, R reinforced" /
  failed. A silent miss is now impossible to miss.

Rebuild, chat a fact-bearing message, and the terminal (cargo tauri dev)
prints exactly what capture did — that tells us if it's path, scope, embedder,
or salience.
